  "theorem_name": "ExactlySevenValuationOnesOtherwiseTwoCycleExclusion",
  "declared_proposition": "No positive accelerated Collatz cycle has a valuation period with exactly seven entries equal to one and every other entry equal to two, including primitive and imprimitive periods.",
  "mathematical_argument": "For such a period of length h, the affine denominator is D=2^(2h-7)-3^h, which is positive from h=17. A nontrivial positive odd cycle cannot contain one, hence each orbit value is at least three. Multiplication around the cycle gives 1<=128(5/6)^h. At h=27 the right side is strictly below one and decreases thereafter. For 17<=h<=26, exhaustive exact enumeration of sum C(h,7)=2,195,765 words finds no affine-divisibility hit.",
